		"title": "BKT belief tracker",
		"html": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Bayesian Knowledge Tracing — Belief Tracker</title>\n<style>\n  :root{\n    --accent:#2563eb;\n    --accent-soft:#dbeafe;\n    --accent-2:#93c5fd;\n    --ink:#1f2937;\n    --muted:#6b7280;\n    --line:#e5e7eb;\n    --panel:#ffffff;\n    --bg:#f6f7f9;\n    --green:#15803d;\n    --green-bg:#ecfdf5;\n    --green-line:#a7f3d0;\n    --red:#b91c1c;\n    --red-bg:#fef2f2;\n    --red-line:#fecaca;\n    --mono: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, \"SF Mono\", Menlo, Consolas, monospace;\n  }\n  *{box-sizing:border-box}\n  html,body{margin:0;padding:0}\n  body{\n    background:var(--bg); color:var(--ink);\n    font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,\"Segoe UI\",Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;\n    font-size:14px; line-height:1.45; padding:18px 18px 26px;\n  }\n  .wrap{max-width:1080px;margin:0 auto}\n  h1{font-size:19px;margin:0 0 3px;letter-spacing:-.01em}\n  .subtitle{color:var(--muted);font-size:13px;margin:0 0 16px}\n  .grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:296px minmax(0,1fr);gap:14px;align-items:start}\n  @media (max-width:840px){ .grid{grid-template-columns:1fr} }\n\n  .panel{\n    background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;\n    padding:14px 14px 16px;box-shadow:0 1px 2px rgba(16,24,40,.04);\n  }\n  .panel + .panel{margin-top:14px}\n  .panel h2{font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.09em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted);margin:0 0 12px;font-weight:700}\n\n  /* ---------- controls ---------- */\n  .ctl{margin-bottom:15px}\n  .ctl .row{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline;gap:8px;margin-bottom:5px}\n  .ctl .name{font-size:13px;font-weight:600}\n  .ctl .val{\n    font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12.5px;font-weight:700;color:var(--accent);\n    background:var(--accent-soft);border-radius:6px;padding:1px 7px;min-width:44px;text-align:center;\n  }\n  .ctl .hint{font-size:11.5px;color:var(--muted);margin-top:4px}\n  input[type=range]{\n    -webkit-appearance:none;appearance:none;width:100%;height:22px;background:transparent;margin:0;cursor:pointer;\n  }\n  input[type=range]::-webkit-slider-runnable-track{height:6px;border-radius:999px;background:#e8ecf2}\n  input[type=range]::-webkit-slider-thumb{\n    -webkit-appearance:none;appearance:none;width:18px;height:18px;border-radius:50%;\n    background:var(--accent);border:2px solid #fff;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,.28);margin-top:-6px;\n  }\n  input[type=range]::-moz-range-track{height:6px;border-radius:999px;background:#e8ecf2}\n  input[type=range]::-moz-range-thumb{width:16px;height:16px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--accent);border:2px solid #fff;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,.28)}\n\n  .btnrow{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:9px;margin-top:4px}\n  .btn{\n    font-family:inherit;font-size:15px;font-weight:700;border-radius:11px;border:1px solid;\n    padding:13px 10px;cursor:pointer;transition:transform .08s,filter .15s,opacity .15s;\n  }\n  .btn:active{transform:translateY(1px)}\n  .btn:disabled{opacity:.45;cursor:default}\n  .btn-correct{background:var(--green-bg);border-color:var(--green-line);color:var(--green)}\n  .btn-wrong{background:var(--red-bg);border-color:var(--red-line);color:var(--red)}\n  .btn-reset{\n    grid-column:1 / -1;background:#f9fafb;border-color:var(--line);color:var(--muted);\n    font-size:13px;font-weight:600;padding:9px;\n  }\n\n  /* ---------- belief readout ---------- */\n  .readout{display:flex;align-items:flex-end;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap}\n  .bigval{font-size:52px;line-height:1;font-weight:750;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;letter-spacing:-.02em}\n  .bigval .lbl{font-size:14px;font-weight:600;color:var(--muted);margin-right:10px;letter-spacing:0}\n  .phaseNow{font-size:12.5px;font-weight:700;color:var(--muted);font-family:var(--mono)}\n  .phaseNow.predict{color:var(--accent)}\n  .phaseNow.correct{color:var(--green)}\n\n  .barwrap{margin-top:14px}\n  .track{\n    position:relative;height:32px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2f7;\n    border:1px solid #e3e8ef;overflow:hidden;\n  }\n  .fill{\n    position:absolute;left:0;top:0;bottom:0;width:30%;\n    background:linear-gradient(90deg,#3b82f6,#2563eb);\n    border-radius:999px 0 0 999px;\n  }\n  .barlegend{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:11.5px;color:var(--muted);margin-top:5px;font-family:var(--mono)}\n  .status{margin-top:10px;font-size:12.5px;color:var(--muted);min-height:19px}\n  .status b{color:var(--ink)}\n\n  /* ---------- phases ---------- */\n  .phases{display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:stretch}\n  .phase{\n    flex:1 1 0;min-width:0;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:10px 12px 12px;\n    background:#fcfdff;opacity:.5;transition:opacity .18s,border-color .18s,box-shadow .18s,background .18s;\n  }\n  .phase.active{opacity:1;border-color:var(--accent);background:#fff;box-shadow:0 0 0 3px var(--accent-soft)}\n  .phase .tag{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;font-size:11px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.1em;color:var(--muted)}\n  .phase.active .tag{color:var(--accent)}\n  .phase .num{\n    display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;width:17px;height:17px;border-radius:50%;\n    background:var(--line);color:#475569;font-size:10.5px;font-weight:800;\n  }\n  .phase.active .num{background:var(--accent);color:#fff}\n  .phase .when{font-size:11px;color:var(--muted);margin-left:2px}\n  .formula{font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12.5px;margin-top:8px;color:#334155}\n  .nums{\n    font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;margin-top:7px;padding-top:7px;border-top:1px dashed var(--line);\n    color:#64748b;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;\n  }\n  .phase.active .nums{color:var(--ink)}\n  .phasearrow{align-self:center;color:#94a3b8;font-size:18px;padding-bottom:6px}\n\n  /* ---------- timeline ---------- */\n  canvas#timeline{display:block;width:100%;height:196px}\n  .tlegend{display:flex;gap:16px;flex-wrap:wrap;font-size:11.5px;color:var(--muted);margin-top:6px}\n  .tlegend span{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px}\n  .swatch{width:18px;height:0;border-top:2px solid var(--accent);display:inline-block}\n  .swatch.dash{border-top:2px dashed var(--accent-2)}\n\n  /* ---------- log ---------- */\n  table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12.5px}\n  th{\n    text-align:right;font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted);\n    font-weight:700;padding:0 6px 6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);\n  }\n  th:first-child,td:first-child{text-align:left}\n  td{padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid #f1f4f8;font-family:var(--mono);text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}\n  td.resp{font-weight:700;text-align:left}\n  tr:last-child td{border-bottom:none}\n  .ok{color:var(--green)}\n  .bad{color:var(--red)}\n  .empty{color:var(--muted);font-family:inherit;text-align:left}\n  .foot{font-size:11.5px;color:var(--muted);margin-top:12px}\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div class=\"wrap\">\n  <h1>Bayesian Knowledge Tracing — Belief Tracker</h1>\n  <p class=\"subtitle\">One skill with a hidden state: the student either <b>knows</b> it (1) or <b>doesn't</b> (0). We only see answers, so we track a belief <b>p = P(knows)</b>. Each attempt updates it in two separate phases: <b>PREDICT</b> (learning may happen) then <b>CORRECT</b> (the observed answer tells us something).</p>\n\n  <div class=\"grid\">\n    <!-- ================= LEFT: CONTROLS ================= -->\n    <div>\n      <div class=\"panel\">\n        <h2>Parameters</h2>\n\n        <div class=\"ctl\">\n          <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"name\">Prior P(knows at start)</span><span class=\"val\" id=\"priorVal\">0.300</span></div>\n          <input type=\"range\" id=\"prior\" min=\"0\" max=\"1\" step=\"0.01\" value=\"0.3\">\n          <div class=\"hint\">Where the belief begins. Changing it restarts the sequence.</div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"ctl\">\n          <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"name\">Learn rate T</span><span class=\"val\" id=\"learnVal\">0.100</span></div>\n          <input type=\"range\" id=\"learn\" min=\"0\" max=\"0.6\" step=\"0.01\" value=\"0.1\">\n          <div class=\"hint\">P(0 → 1) between attempts: chance of picking up the skill.</div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"ctl\">\n          <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"name\">Slip s</span><span class=\"val\" id=\"slipVal\">0.100</span></div>\n          <input type=\"range\" id=\"slip\" min=\"0\" max=\"0.5\" step=\"0.01\" value=\"0.1\">\n          <div class=\"hint\">P(wrong | knows).</div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"ctl\">\n          <div class=\"row\"><span class=\"name\">Guess g</span><span class=\"val\" id=\"guessVal\">0.200</span></div>\n          <input type=\"range\" id=\"guess\" min=\"0\" max=\"0.5\" step=\"0.01\" value=\"0.2\">\n          <div class=\"hint\">P(correct | doesn't know).</div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"panel\">\n        <h2>Observed response</h2>\n        <div class=\"btnrow\">\n          <button class=\"btn btn-correct\" id=\"btnCorrect\">Correct</button>\n          <button class=\"btn btn-wrong\" id=\"btnWrong\">Incorrect</button>\n          <button class=\"btn btn-reset\" id=\"btnReset\">Reset — back to prior, clear history</button>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"foot\">Each press runs one attempt: PREDICT first, then CORRECT.</div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <!-- ================= RIGHT: DISPLAY ================= -->\n    <div>\n      <div class=\"panel\">\n        <h2>Current belief</h2>\n        <div class=\"readout\">\n          <div class=\"bigval\"><span class=\"lbl\">P(knows) =</span><span id=\"bigval\">0.300</span></div>\n          <div class=\"phaseNow\" id=\"phaseNow\">phase: idle</div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"barwrap\">\n          <div class=\"track\"><div class=\"fill\" id=\"fill\"></div></div>\n          <div class=\"barlegend\"><span>0.0</span><span>0.5</span><span>1.0</span></div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"status\" id=\"status\">Ready — press <b>Correct</b> or <b>Incorrect</b> to run attempt #1.</div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"panel\">\n        <h2>The two updates</h2>\n        <div class=\"phases\">\n          <div class=\"phase\" id=\"phasePredict\">\n            <div class=\"tag\"><span class=\"num\">1</span>PREDICT<span class=\"when\">— allow learning</span></div>\n            <div class=\"formula\">p&#772; = p + T&#183;(1 &minus; p)</div>\n            <div class=\"nums\" id=\"predictNums\">—</div>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"phasearrow\">&rarr;</div>\n          <div class=\"phase\" id=\"phaseCorrect\">\n            <div class=\"tag\"><span class=\"num\">2</span>CORRECT<span class=\"when\">— use the response</span></div>\n            <div class=\"formula\" id=\"correctFormula\">p&prime; = (1&minus;s)&#183;p&#772; / [ (1&minus;s)&#183;p&#772; + g&#183;(1&minus;p&#772;) ]</div>\n            <div class=\"nums\" id=\"correctNums\">—</div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"panel\">\n        <h2>Belief over attempts</h2>\n        <canvas id=\"timeline\"></canvas>\n        <div class=\"tlegend\">\n          <span><span class=\"swatch\"></span> belief p after each attempt</span>\n          <span><span class=\"swatch dash\"></span> p&#772; straight after PREDICT</span>\n          <span>filled dot = P(knows) &nbsp; C/W = observed response</span>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"panel\">\n        <h2>Attempt log (most recent first)</h2>\n        <table>\n          <thead>\n            <tr><th>#</th><th>Response</th><th>p (before)</th><th>p&#772; (predict)</th><th>p&prime; (after)</th></tr>\n          </thead>\n          <tbody id=\"logBody\"><tr><td colspan=\"5\" class=\"empty\">No attempts yet.</td></tr></tbody>\n        </table>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<script>\n(function(){\n  \"use strict\";\n\n  var el = function(id){ return document.getElementById(id); };\n  var fmt = function(v){ return (Math.round(v*1000)/1000).toFixed(3); };\n  var clamp01 = function(v){ return v < 0 ? 0 : (v > 1 ? 1 : v); };\n  var MONO = 'ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace';\n\n  var state = {\n    p: 0.3,\n    history: [],   // {n, resp, pBefore, pBar, pAfter}\n    busy: false,\n    phase: 'idle'\n  };\n\n  function params(){\n    return {\n      prior: parseFloat(el('prior').value),\n      T: parseFloat(el('learn').value),\n      s: parseFloat(el('slip').value),\n      g: parseFloat(el('guess').value)\n    };\n  }\n\n  /* ---------------- rendering ---------------- */\n\n  function renderBelief(v){\n    var x = clamp01(v);\n    el('bigval').textContent = fmt(x);\n    el('fill').style.width = (x*100).toFixed(2) + '%';\n  }\n\n  function setPhase(phase, statusText){\n    state.phase = phase;\n    el('phasePredict').classList.toggle('active', phase === 'predict');\n    el('phaseCorrect').classList.toggle('active', phase === 'correct');\n    var pn = el('phaseNow');\n    pn.className = 'phaseNow' + (phase === 'idle' ? '' : ' ' + phase);\n    pn.textContent = 'phase: ' + (phase === 'idle' ? 'idle' : (phase === 'predict' ? '1 PREDICT' : '2 CORRECT'));\n    if (statusText !== undefined){\n      el('status').innerHTML = statusText;\n    }\n  }\n\n  function predictNumbersText(p, T, pBar){\n    return '= ' + fmt(p) + ' + ' + fmt(T) + ' \\u00d7 (1 \\u2212 ' + fmt(p) + ')\\n'\n         + '= ' + fmt(p) + ' + ' + fmt(T*(1-p)) + ' = ' + fmt(pBar);\n  }\n\n  function correctNumbersText(resp, pBar, s, g, num, den, pAfter){\n    var lines;\n    if (resp === 'C'){\n      lines = 'numerator  (1 \\u2212 s)\\u00b7p\\u0304 = (1 \\u2212 ' + fmt(s) + ') \\u00d7 ' + fmt(pBar) + ' = ' + fmt(num)\n            + '\\ndenominator  ' + fmt(num) + ' + g\\u00b7(1 \\u2212 p\\u0304) = ' + fmt(num) + ' + ' + fmt(g) + ' \\u00d7 ' + fmt(1-pBar) + ' = ' + fmt(den);\n    } else {\n      lines = 'numerator  s\\u00b7p\\u0304 = ' + fmt(s) + ' \\u00d7 ' + fmt(pBar) + ' = ' + fmt(num)\n            + '\\ndenominator  ' + fmt(num) + ' + (1 \\u2212 g)\\u00b7(1 \\u2212 p\\u0304) = ' + fmt(num) + ' + ' + fmt(1-g) + ' \\u00d7 ' + fmt(1-pBar) + ' = ' + fmt(den);\n    }\n    lines += '\\np\\u2032 = ' + fmt(num) + ' / ' + fmt(den) + ' = ' + fmt(pAfter);\n    return lines;\n  }\n\n  function formulaFor(resp){\n    return resp === 'C'\n      ? 'p\\u2032 = (1\\u2212s)\\u00b7p\\u0304 / [ (1\\u2212s)\\u00b7p\\u0304 + g\\u00b7(1\\u2212p\\u0304) ]'\n      : 'p\\u2032 = s\\u00b7p\\u0304 / [ s\\u00b7p\\u0304 + (1\\u2212g)\\u00b7(1\\u2212p\\u0304) ]';\n  }\n\n  function renderLog(){\n    var body = el('logBody');\n    if (!state.history.length){\n      body.innerHTML = '<tr><td colspan=\"5\" class=\"empty\">No attempts yet.</td></tr>';\n      return;\n    }\n    var rows = state.history.slice(-6).reverse().map(function(r){\n      var cls = r.resp === 'C' ? 'ok' : 'bad';\n      var word = r.resp === 'C' ? 'Correct' : 'Wrong';\n      return '<tr>'\n        + '<td>' + r.n + '</td>'\n        + '<td class=\"resp ' + cls + '\">' + word + '</td>'\n        + '<td>' + fmt(r.pBefore) + '</td>'\n        + '<td>' + fmt(r.pBar) + '</td>'\n        + '<td><b>' + fmt(r.pAfter) + '</b></td>'\n        + '</tr>';\n    }).join('');\n    body.innerHTML = rows;\n  }\n\n  /* ---------------- timeline canvas ---------------- */\n\n  function drawTimeline(){\n    var c = el('timeline');\n    if (!c) return;\n    var dpr = window.devicePixelRatio || 1;\n    var w = c.clientWidth || 600;\n    var h = c.clientHeight || 196;\n    c.width = Math.max(1, Math.round(w*dpr));\n    c.height = Math.max(1, Math.round(h*dpr));\n    var ctx = c.getContext('2d');\n    ctx.setTransform(dpr,0,0,dpr,0,0);\n    ctx.clearRect(0,0,w,h);\n\n    var padL = 40, padR = 18, padT = 16, padB = 36;\n    var pw = Math.max(10, w - padL - padR);\n    var ph = Math.max(10, h - padT - padB);\n    var attempts = state.history.length;\n    var slots = Math.max(10, attempts);\n    var X = function(i){ return padL + pw * (i / slots); };\n    var Y = function(v){ return padT + ph * (1 - clamp01(v)); };\n\n    // grid + y labels\n    ctx.lineWidth = 1;\n    ctx.font = '11px ' + MONO;\n    ctx.textAlign = 'right';\n    ctx.textBaseline = 'middle';\n    for (var k = 0; k <= 4; k++){\n      var v = k/4, y = Y(v);\n      ctx.strokeStyle = (k===0 || k===4) ? '#dfe5ec' : '#eef1f5';\n      ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(padL, y); ctx.lineTo(padL+pw, y); ctx.stroke();\n      ctx.fillStyle = '#9aa3af';\n      ctx.fillText(v.toFixed(2), padL - 8, y);\n    }\n\n    // build series\n    var prior = params().prior;\n    var pts = [{ i:0, p: prior, pBar: null, resp: null }];\n    for (var j = 0; j < attempts; j++){\n      var r = state.history[j];\n      pts.push({ i: j+1, p: r.pAfter, pBar: r.pBar, resp: r.resp });\n    }\n\n    // p-bar dashed series (skip first point)\n    if (pts.length > 1){\n      ctx.save();\n      ctx.setLineDash([5,4]);\n      ctx.strokeStyle = '#93c5fd';\n      ctx.lineWidth = 1.6;\n      ctx.beginPath();\n      // from prior directly to first p-bar would be misleading; start at first attempt's pBar\n      ctx.moveTo(X(pts[1].i), Y(pts[1].pBar));\n      for (var m = 2; m < pts.length; m++){\n        ctx.lineTo(X(pts[m].i), Y(pts[m].pBar));\n      }\n      ctx.stroke();\n      ctx.restore();\n      for (var q = 1; q < pts.length; q++){\n        ctx.beginPath();\n        ctx.arc(X(pts[q].i), Y(pts[q].pBar), 3.2, 0, Math.PI*2);\n        ctx.fillStyle = '#fff';\n        ctx.fill();\n        ctx.strokeStyle = '#93c5fd';\n        ctx.lineWidth = 1.6;\n        ctx.stroke();\n      }\n    }\n\n    // belief solid series\n    ctx.strokeStyle = '#2563eb';\n    ctx.lineWidth = 2.2;\n    ctx.beginPath();\n    ctx.moveTo(X(pts[0].i), Y(pts[0].p));\n    for (var n2 = 1; n2 < pts.length; n2++){\n      ctx.lineTo(X(pts[n2].i), Y(pts[n2].p));\n    }\n    ctx.stroke();\n\n    // dots + response letters\n    ctx.textAlign = 'center';\n    for (var d = 0; d < pts.length; d++){\n      var pt = pts[d];\n      var x = X(pt.i), y = Y(pt.p);\n      ctx.beginPath();\n      ctx.arc(x, y, d === 0 ? 4.2 : 4.6, 0, Math.PI*2);\n      ctx.fillStyle = d === 0 ? '#94a3b8' : '#2563eb';\n      ctx.fill();\n      ctx.strokeStyle = '#fff';\n      ctx.lineWidth = 1.6;\n      ctx.stroke();\n\n      if (d === 0){\n        ctx.fillStyle = '#9aa3af';\n        ctx.font = '10.5px ' + MONO;\n        ctx.fillText('start', x, padT + ph + 16);\n        ctx.fillStyle = '#64748b';\n        ctx.fillText(fmt(pt.p), x, y - 12);\n      } else {\n        ctx.font = 'bold 11.5px ' + MONO;\n        ctx.fillStyle = pt.resp === 'C' ? '#15803d' : '#b91c1c';\n        ctx.fillText(pt.resp === 'C' ? 'C' : 'W', x, padT + ph + 18);\n        ctx.font = '10.5px ' + MONO;\n        ctx.fillStyle = '#475569';\n        ctx.fillText(fmt(pt.p), x, y - 12);\n      }\n    }\n\n    if (attempts === 0){\n      ctx.textAlign = 'left';\n      ctx.font = '12px -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, sans-serif';\n      ctx.fillStyle = '#9aa3af';\n      ctx.fillText('Run an attempt to start the trace \\u2192', padL + 14, Y(prior) - 26);\n    }\n  }\n\n  /* ---------------- animation ---------------- */\n\n  function animate(from, to, dur, onFrame, onDone){\n    var t0 = performance.now();\n    function step(now){\n      var t = (now - t0) / dur;\n      if (t > 1) t = 1;\n      var e = t < 0.5 ? 2*t*t : 1 - Math.pow(-2*t + 2, 2)/2; // easeInOutQuad\n      onFrame(from + (to - from) * e);\n      if (t < 1) requestAnimationFrame(step);\n      else if (onDone) onDone();\n    }\n    requestAnimationFrame(step);\n  }\n\n  function setBusy(b){\n    state.busy = b;\n    el('btnCorrect').disabled = b;\n    el('btnWrong').disabled = b;\n    el('btnReset').disabled = b;\n  }\n\n  function doAttempt(resp){\n    if (state.busy) return;\n    setBusy(true);\n\n    var pr = params();\n    var T = pr.T, s = pr.s, g = pr.g;\n    var pBefore = state.p;\n    var pBar = pBefore + T * (1 - pBefore);\n    var num, den, pAfter;\n    if (resp === 'C'){\n      num = (1 - s) * pBar;\n      den = num + g * (1 - pBar);\n    } else {\n      num = s * pBar;\n      den = num + (1 - g) * (1 - pBar);\n    }\n    pAfter = den === 0 ? 0 : num / den;\n    pBar = clamp01(pBar); pAfter = clamp01(pAfter);\n\n    var rec = { n: state.history.length + 1, resp: resp, pBefore: pBefore, pBar: pBar, pAfter: pAfter };\n\n    // ---- PHASE 1: PREDICT ----\n    setPhase('predict', 'Phase 1 \\u2014 <b>PREDICT</b>: the student may learn between attempts, so belief moves up from '\n      + fmt(pBefore) + ' to p\\u0304 = ' + fmt(pBar) + '.');\n    el('correctFormula').innerHTML = resp === 'C'\n      ? 'p\\u2032 = (1\\u2212s)\\u00b7p\\u0304 / [ (1\\u2212s)\\u00b7p\\u0304 + g\\u00b7(1\\u2212p\\u0304) ]'\n      : 'p\\u2032 = s\\u00b7p\\u0304 / [ s\\u00b7p\\u0304 + (1\\u2212g)\\u00b7(1\\u2212p\\u0304) ]';\n    el('predictNums').textContent = predictNumbersText(pBefore, T, pBar);\n    el('correctNums').textContent = 'waiting for the response\\u2026';\n    renderBelief(pBefore);\n\n    animate(pBefore, pBar, 520, renderBelief, function(){\n      renderBelief(pBar);\n      // ---- PHASE 2: CORRECT ----\n      window.setTimeout(function(){\n        setPhase('correct', 'Phase 2 \\u2014 <b>CORRECT</b>: the response was <b>' + (resp === 'C' ? 'Correct' : 'Incorrect')\n          + '</b>, so Bayes\\u2019 rule moves belief from p\\u0304 = ' + fmt(pBar) + ' to p\\u2032 = ' + fmt(pAfter) + '.');\n        el('correctNums').textContent = correctNumbersText(resp, pBar, s, g, num, den, pAfter);\n        animate(pBar, pAfter, 620, renderBelief, function(){\n          renderBelief(pAfter);\n          state.p = pAfter;\n          state.history.push(rec);\n          renderLog();\n          drawTimeline();\n          setPhase('idle', 'Attempt #' + rec.n + ' done (' + (resp === 'C' ? 'Correct' : 'Incorrect') + '). Belief is now <b>'\n            + fmt(pAfter) + '</b>. Press an answer button for attempt #' + (rec.n + 1) + '.');\n          setBusy(false);\n        });\n      }, 340);\n    });\n  }\n\n  function reset(){\n    if (state.busy) return;\n    var pr = params();\n    state.p = pr.prior;\n    state.history = [];\n    el('predictNums').textContent = predictNumbersText(state.p, pr.T, state.p + pr.T*(1-state.p));\n    el('correctNums').innerHTML = '<span style=\"color:#94a3b8\">Press <b>Correct</b> or <b>Incorrect</b> to apply this step.</span>';\n    el('correctFormula').textContent = 'p\\u2032 = (1\\u2212s)\\u00b7p\\u0304 / [ (1\\u2212s)\\u00b7p\\u0304 + g\\u00b7(1\\u2212p\\u0304) ]   (correct)';\n    renderBelief(state.p);\n    renderLog();\n    drawTimeline();\n    setPhase('idle', 'Reset \\u2014 belief back to the prior, history cleared. Press an answer button to run attempt #1.');\n  }\n\n  /* idle preview: show what PREDICT would do right now */\n  function refreshPreview(){\n    if (state.busy) return;\n    var pr = params();\n    var pBar = state.p + pr.T * (1 - state.p);\n    el('predictNums').textContent = predictNumbersText(state.p, pr.T, pBar);\n  }\n\n  /* ---------------- wiring ---------------- */\n\n  function syncSlider(id, out, digits){\n    var inp = el(id);\n    var show = function(){ el(out).textContent = parseFloat(inp.value).toFixed(digits); };\n    inp.addEventListener('input', function(){\n      show();\n      if (id === 'prior'){\n        reset();\n      } else {\n        refreshPreview();\n      }\n    });\n    show();\n  }\n\n  syncSlider('prior', 'priorVal', 3);\n  syncSlider('learn', 'learnVal', 3);\n  syncSlider('slip', 'slipVal', 3);\n  syncSlider('guess', 'guessVal', 3);\n\n  el('btnCorrect').addEventListener('click', function(){ doAttempt('C'); });\n  el('btnWrong').addEventListener('click', function(){ doAttempt('W'); });\n  el('btnReset').addEventListener('click', reset);\n\n  window.addEventListener('resize', drawTimeline);\n  window.addEventListener('load', function(){ drawTimeline(); });\n\n  // initial paint\n  reset();\n\n  // test hook\n  window.__demo = {\n    state: state,\n    params: params,\n    doAttempt: doAttempt,\n    reset: reset,\n    drawTimeline: drawTimeline,\n    prevCorrect: function(r){ return r.pBar*(1-params().s) / (r.pBar*(1-params().s) + (1-r.pBar)*params().g); }\n  };\n})();\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n",
		"tested": true,
		"notes": "The demo is built and verified — all three headless runs passed with no console errors, and the probe checks confirm the arithmetic matches Bayes' rule exactly (e.g. p=0.300 → p̄=0.370 → 0.725 on \"Correct\", and 0.068 on \"Incorrect\" with the defaults).\n\n**Notes for the teacher**\n\n- **What it shows:** a single-skill BKT belief tracker — one big P(knows) number (3 decimals) plus a filled bar, a two-panel \"PREDICT → CORRECT\" strip with live formulas/numerator/denominator, a belief sparkline over attempts (dashed = p̄ after predict, solid = p after correct, each attempt marked C or W), and a short log of the last six attempts (response, p, p̄, p′).\n- **Controls:** four sliders — Prior (0–1, default 0.30), Learn rate T (0–0.6, default 0.10), Slip s (0–0.5, default 0.10), Guess g (0–0.5, default 0.20) — plus **Correct**, **Incorrect**, and **Reset**. Each answer press animates the two phases in sequence with the active panel highlighted and the status line narrating which operation is running, so the two updates are visibly separate.\n- **Try this:** press Incorrect three times and watch belief crater toward 0 (each subsequent wrong answer barely dents it once the denominator is dominated by the leak), then press Correct twice to see recovery; set Slip = 0 and Guess = 0 to make the evidence \"hard\"; or set T = 0 to isolate pure Bayesian correction. Note that moving the Prior slider intentionally restarts the whole sequence."
	}
